{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows low positivity (0.00) and true prices exhibit strong mean reversion or downward drift.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes — if true price rises sharply after a low sentiment period, anticipate overshoot and adjust downward by 5-10% in next period.",
    "When sentiment history includes a recent 0.33 (moderate bullish), model should not overreact — cap forecast increases to avoid overestimating upward momentum.",
    "For long-term (30-day) forecasts, apply mean reversion bias: if model consistently overpredicts above 70, reduce forecast by 3-5% to align with historical volatility.",
    "If true price drops below 65 after a spike, assume sentiment shift — reduce forecast by 10-15% to reflect cooling market sentiment.",
    "Avoid forecasting upward trends when sentiment history is flat (all 0.00) and recent prices are trending downward — use conservative, lagged mean as anchor."
  ]
}
